tasks.description:
**Goal:** Every read of `closing` in the references reads only the key it uses, except close step 1's own-phase `rulings` check. Writes that change a few lines use `edit`.

**Files:**
- Modify: `skills/chaining-plans/references/close.md`
  - the rules of step 0 on reading `closing`;
  - the discard;
  - the sort of `unfinished` at the end of step 1;
  - step 1a;
  - the moves of step 2.
- Modify: `skills/chaining-plans/references/resume.md`
  - § 5 "Read the items";
  - the writes of the suffixes;
  - the `[settled: …]` write in "Answers given outside a round".
- Modify: `skills/chaining-plans/references/create.md` (step 5, the carried items)
- Test: `tests/chaining-plans/test-close-text.sh`, `test-resume-text.sh`, `test-carry-text.sh`

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] `grep -rn 'get REC [^ ]* closing\`\|get <record> <phase> closing\`' skills/chaining-plans/references` finds no read of the whole `closing`.
- [ ] Close 1a reads `closing.learned`, and writes with `learned edit` (drops, and corrections as `[old, new]`).
- [ ] Close 2 rewrites each moved `unfinished` line as its pointer with `unfinished edit`.
- [ ] The resume suffix writes and the create carried-item write use `unfinished edit`, with the line exactly as read and the same line with its suffix.
- [ ] Closes keep `replace` for the first `learned` write, the sort of `unfinished`, the discard and `replan`.
- [ ] New pins:
  - `test-close-text.sh` has `learned edit` and `closing.learned`;
  - `test-resume-text.sh` lacks `unfinished replace`;
  - `test-carry-text.sh` has `unfinished edit` in `create.md`.

**Verify:** `for t in tests/chaining-plans/test-*.sh tests/reference-ids/test-reference-ids.sh; do bash "$t" >/dev/null || echo "FAIL $t"; done` → no output

The steps are in docs/superpowers/plans/G1.md, Task G1.3.

